__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# The monorepo scaffold (P1). node_modules had no entry here until packages
# existed to install into, and an untracked-but-not-ignored node_modules is a
# `git status` nobody can read and an accidental commit waiting to happen.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Coverage OUTPUT, not a coverage gate. Coverage is reported per package as a
# trend and is not a merge blocker anywhere (STRATEGY section 2); RI-02 asserts
# that no threshold exists in the tree.
coverage/

.DS_Store

# `scripts/ci/falsify-ci.mjs`'s crash journal. It holds the pre-seed contents of
# whatever file a mutant is currently sitting on, so a killed run can be undone
# by the next one. It exists only while a case is in flight and must never be
# committed: it is a copy of tracked source, and a stale copy at that.
.falsify-pending.json

# `CI-08`'s runner output. Playwright writes `test-results/` on a failure (a
# trace, a screenshot, the error context) and `playwright-report/` when an HTML
# reporter is selected. Both are artifacts OF a run rather than inputs to one,
# and a committed trace is a stale copy of a rendering nobody can reproduce.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# `next-env.d.ts`, which `next build` WRITES rather than reads. Next.js
# regenerates it on every build from a template it owns, and the file says so in
# its own body: "This file should not be edited". Committing it would put a
# generated file under `prettier --check`, which reformats it, which the next
# build undoes: a gate that goes red on a clean build is the failure mode
# `.next/` is already ignored to avoid. Nothing in this workspace reads it
# either, because no `tsconfig` `include` names it and `pnpm run typecheck`
# passes without it (measured, session 250). It is an artifact OF a run and not
# an input to one, which is this file's own test one entry up.
next-env.d.ts

# `CI-09`'s Stryker leg working directory. Stryker copies the package into
# `.stryker-tmp/sandbox-*` and mutates the COPY, which is what keeps a mutation
# run from being the tree-mutating operation `falsify:ci` has to be. It is
# removed at the end of a run that finishes and SURVIVES A CRASH, which is
# exactly when a `git add -A` would sweep a directory of half-mutated source
# into a commit.
#
# AND THIS LINE DOES LESS THAN IT LOOKS LIKE IT DOES, WHICH IS WORTH KNOWING
# BEFORE IT SURPRISES SOMEBODY. `gates.mjs`'s `walk` skips `node_modules` and
# `.git` and nothing else, so an ignored directory is still READ by every CI-06
# gate: a crashed mutation run leaves `pnpm run verify` red over copies of files
# already in the tree, 427 CI-06a findings and 35 CI-06/retired-constraints
# findings when it was measured. Deleting the directory is the whole repair.
# ADR-127 finding 3; the fix is a gate edit nobody has taken.
.stryker-tmp/

# ENVIRONMENT FILES, AND THE THREE LINES ARE A DERIVED SET RATHER THAN A COPIED
# ONE. `INFRA` section 7 puts every credential in the platform vault and injects
# it at run time, so no file of environment VALUES belongs in this tree at all.
# `INFRA:145` claimed for months that this rule already existed and that `VG-1`
# verified it; both halves were false, and `RI-21` is the half that matters
# (ADR-224).
#
# WHY THREE PATTERNS AND NOT ONE.
#   `.env` carries no slash, so git matches it by BASENAME at any depth: it
#   covers `apps/api/.env` and `packages/db/.env` as well as the root file. A
#   leading-slash `/.env` would have been root-only, which is the spelling that
#   leaves a per-package file uncovered.
#   `.env.*` is the suffix family and it is a SEPARATE pattern because `.env`
#   does not match `.env.local` and `*.env` does not match `.env`. It covers
#   `.env.local`, `.env.production`, `.env.test` and the two-suffix
#   `.env.production.local` spelling, at any depth.
#   `!.env.example` re-includes the one file that is a TEMPLATE rather than a
#   value store. The exception set has exactly one member on purpose: every
#   additional spelling admitted here (`.env.sample`, `.env.template`) is
#   another name under which somebody can commit a real value and be told by
#   this file that it was fine.
#
# `.envrc` IS DELIBERATELY NOT COVERED, and it is named here so the omission
# reads as a decision rather than an oversight. It is direnv's file, direnv is
# used by nothing in this repository (absent from `package.json`, `.github/**`,
# `scripts/**` and every workspace manifest), and it is a shell SCRIPT rather
# than a value file. ADR-224 registers it: the day direnv is adopted, that entry
# is where the pattern set is re-argued.
#
# AND THE ENTRY IS NOT THE CONTROL. Anybody can delete these three lines and no
# gate would notice, which is exactly the defect ADR-224 was written for. `RI-21`
# in `packages/tooling/checks/repo-invariants.mjs` asks `git check-ignore` what
# the rule SAYS about a list of representative paths, so deleting a line here
# turns CI-01 red rather than turning this comment into fiction.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
